  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many more pages Cristobal read compared to Beatrix, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of pages Beatrix read.\n2. Calculate the number of pages Cristobal read based on the information given.\n3. Find the difference between the number of pages Cristobal read and the number of pages Beatrix read.\n\nStep 1: Identify the number of pages Beatrix read.\nBeatrix read 704 pages.\n\nStep 2: Calculate the number of pages Cristobal read.\nCristobal read 15 more than three times the pages that Beatrix read. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ \\text{Number of pages Cristobal read} = 3 \\times \\text{Number of pages Beatrix read} + 15 \\]\nSubstituting the number of pages Beatrix read into the equation:\n\\[ \\text{Number of pages Cristobal read} = 3 \\times 704 + 15 \\]\nFirst, calculate \\(3 \\times 704\\):\n\\[ 3 \\times 704 = 2112 \\]\nThen, add 15 to 2112:\n\\[ 2112 + 15 = 2127 \\]\nSo, Cristobal read 2127 pages.\n\nStep 3: Find the difference between the number of pages Cristobal read and the number of pages Beatrix read.\n\\[ \\text{Difference} = \\text{Number of pages Cristobal read} - \\text{Number of pages Beatrix read} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Difference} = 2127 - 704 \\]\nSubtract 704 from 2127:\n\\[ 2127 - 704 = 1423 \\]\nSo, Cristobal read 1423 more pages than Beatrix.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{1423} \\]",
